Save states compressed as they are serialized and decompressed as they are read: the whole state never sits in memory
uncompressed (nor copied), which a 2 GB device cannot spare beside the running game. The save serializes twice, first
to count the bytes, so the ZSTD frame records its size and the file is the same as before.

